Purpose: Install extensions listed in extensions/preinstalled.toml via an external-provider-style loader (user-removable, removal sticky).
Area: extensions
Files: chrome/browser/extensions/external_provider_impl.cc (CreateExternalProviders, one ExternalPrefLoader provider on DIR_EXTERNAL_EXTENSIONS)
Rebase risk: medium
Origin: original (written for Corvid; no third-party patch text reused)
Status: BUILT and tested on 155.0.8059.39 (option A, 2026-10-14). Unit tests pass; on a fresh profile under Xvfb uBlock Origin 1.75.0 (MV2) installs from <exe dir>/extensions/<id>.json and runs. Not tested: removal staying removed after a restart, in-browser updates (the CRX update path for a non-store extension is untraced).

Change: in ExternalProviderImpl::CreateExternalProviders, after the Drive migration provider, add one ExternalProviderImpl on an ExternalPrefLoader(chrome::DIR_EXTERNAL_EXTENSIONS, NONE, nullptr) with location kExternalPref / kExternalPrefDownload and flags WAS_INSTALLED_BY_DEFAULT (no FROM_WEBSTORE: the CRX is not from the store). DIR_EXTERNAL_EXTENSIONS is <module dir>/extensions on Linux (/opt/<slug>/extensions in packages). The stock per-user and system-wide external extension directories stay disabled by debrand/0180; this adds only the install directory. Loader format: <id>.json = {"external_crx": "<file in that dir>", "external_version": "x.y.z"}; relative CRX paths resolve against the directory. Removal is remembered by the existing extensions.external_uninstalls pref.
Build step: docs/notes/preinstalled-build-step.md; scripts/gen-preinstalled.py emits the JSON; scripts/package.sh copies the JSON and CRX into <install dir>/extensions.
Key custody: the extension id derives from the packing key; test packages use a throwaway key and must not be distributed.

Verify:
- 07-ubo.mjs

